cept", "title": "dynamic control"}], "description": "Students learn to play with healthy movement, evenness, articulation, and musical sound."}]}, {"id": "c8df773b-179d-48d3-9cd8-a2f819811943", "type": "topic", "title": "Reading in Both Clefs", "description": "Music majors need functional fluency in treble and bass clefs for theory, rehearsal, accompanying, and score study.", "children": [{"id": "d81b6dd3-bbdf-4f4a-8021-3a7ba187d3c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grand staff reading", "children": [{"id": "80d42282-9cf9-47b9-ae6b-ec7fa2f48bfa", "type": "concept", "title": "treble clef"}, {"id": "913dfd2f-54d9-451e-aa2d-5887dee4264a", "type": "concept", "title": "bass clef"}, {"id": "495de182-d282-4376-a9ce-bbe8c0dfd310", "type": "concept", "title": "staff relationships"}], "description": "Students practice reading both staves as one coordinated musical system."}, {"id": "e79d4712-9925-46e3-8253-38e46dfb3e1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhythm and coordination", "children": [{"id": "90a8a9cf-63fd-4478-9737-b9a030f5ff0f", "type": "concept", "title": "counting systems"}, {"id": "d963c3ab-8beb-49f8-af4d-cb9ba789151d", "type": "concept", "title": "ties and rests"}, {"id": "b38988dd-bc65-4764-842e-d3e716e73039", "type": "concept", "title": "hands-together rhythm"}], "description": "The class links pitch reading with steady pulse, subdivision, and two-hand independence."}, {"id": "72128dee-9726-4499-9bee-b992dee28ba8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Score-reading habits", "children": [{"id": "c4a2f3dc-8bf6-470a-b9ee-440ee3f08ea2", "type": "concept", "title": "key signature scan"}, {"id": "f8ef9fcb-6466-459f-8c3e-a06ada93c874", "type": "concept", "title": "pattern spotting"}, {"id": "39d535ac-aa8f-4b7f-a0ad-055e3158a621", "type": "concept", "title": "fingering decisions"}], "description": "Students learn previewing strategies that make unfamiliar music less overwhelming."}]}, {"id": "c47c39e8-55c9-4b01-8543-84616c51a7fb", "type": "topic", "title": "Chord Progressions and Cadences", "description": "This unit gives students the keyboard harmony needed for theory application, accompaniment, and functional musicianship.", "children": [{"id": "dad01be4-421e-4f4a-9d43-ccf5b3fcfbb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Triads and inversions", "children": [{"id": "36a1b3ec-5076-4307-8d72-2c9d6c49871e", "type": "concept", "title": "root position"}, {"id": "63d36881-77b6-4b1f-91f4-dc54563e375e", "type": "concept", "title": "first inversion"}, {"id": "a6f7685b-d9b2-4b45-bcfd-da4e5d4cd8f9", "type": "concept", "title": "second inversion"}], "description": "Students learn to build and play chords smoothly in multiple positions."}, {"id": "c7c88d9f-d38c-4fbb-96db-a5b378d93bad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Primary progressions", "children": [{"id": "ad251adb-e5b2-4ed0-baa1-ce21789927d0", "type": "concept", "title": "I-IV-V-I"}, {"id": "3b8230eb-257f-435c-867e-06716466a383", "type": "concept", "title": "ii-V-I awareness"}, {"id": "e8066848-2d99-404c-856e-e088a7b70f32", "type": "concept", "title": "minor-key cadences"}], "description": "The class practices I, IV, V, and V7 progressions in common major and minor keys."}, {"id": "142ba35c-76f0-4f04-9e9a-25ba704bf58d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cadence types", "children": [{"id": "b0969628-7e6e-4cfd-8879-df411a96082b", "type": "concept", "title": "authentic cadence"}, {"id": "36387343-b38d-44f6-936f-a4143f198f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "half cadence"}, {"id": "3d845971-6d51-48cc-81ca-0f1c026d56ea", "type": "concept", "title": "plagal cadence"}], "description": "Students connect harmonic closure to musical phrase structure and style."}]}, {"id": "51369259-ed6c-469c-8486-58fa7cb08d96", "type": "topic", "title": "Harmonization of Melodies", "description": "Harmonization turns theoretical chord knowledge into practical keyboard musicianship for teaching, arranging, and rehearsal work.", "children": [{"id": "c11678f0-64c7-4622-bddf-17a40909728c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Harmonic analysis of simple melodies", "children": [{"id": "de6b0677-f61a-4338-a6fc-11716f26d1bc", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase endings"}, {"id": "6e955f24-a68c-4e70-94d7-e93ea45289ef", "type": "concept", "title": "non-chord tones"}, {"id": "bc65e32e-b753-4359-a523-f2d8c10d2fc1", "type": "concept", "title": "harmonic rhythm"}], "description": "Students identify phrase points, implied harmonies, and cadential goals."}, {"id": "54bb7c02-0c9d-4c3d-a880-6dd859d13dcb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Block-chord harmonization", "children": [{"id": "11f99a0c-8a47-4c2a-bd5f-e7b2f7cbb682", "type": "concept", "title": "root-position chords"}, {"id": "0401250f-abb0-447d-adf1-dcda5e609f4d", "type": "concept", "title": "inverted chords"}, {"id": "14db1d17-74c3-4d62-9b98-50600d349112", "type": "concept", "title": "voice leading"}], "description": "The unit begins with simple left-hand or two-hand chord settings."}, {"id": "52e50bb1-b443-4520-ac5b-99cf85beab20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Style-appropriate realization", "children": [{"id": "b39a1e44-4a7c-42f6-a835-27c8031e97a8", "type": "concept", "title": "broken chords"}, {"id": "3611bc8c-5937-42c9-baec-208f7e47265c", "type": "concept", "title": "waltz bass"}, {"id": "0053ef26-14e7-4e9c-81a7-7d05bc619e19", "type": "concept", "title": "lead-sheet symbols"}], "description": "Students experiment with accompaniments that fit folk, classical, pop, and classroom settings."}]}, {"id": "775d8aa1-0994-45cd-bb21-fc4c2d11ef3a", "type": "topic", "title": "Sight-Reading", "description": "Sight-reading develops practical fluency: the ability to keep going musically while processing unfamiliar notation.", "children": [{"id": "d0b04398-516a-4129-91de-f115015f2f2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Preview strategy", "children": [{"id": "43df54a7-faf0-4f9e-b162-21b54ef2df6d", "type": "concept", "title": "key and meter"}, {"id": "a122c294-f09f-432f-9f62-29d150e79de9", "type": "concept", "title": "hand position"}, {"id": "050e87f3-1cd3-41c8-8889-52f9d4e495fb", "type"